  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FCR">Lemma <span data-tag="0FCR">13.28.4</span>.</a> Let $H : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{A}$ be a homological functor from a triangulated category to an abelian category. Assume that for any $X$ in $\mathcal{D}$ only a finite number of the objects $H(X[i])$ are nonzero in $\mathcal{A}$. Then $H$ induces a group homomorphism $K_0(\mathcal{D}) \to K_0(\mathcal{A})$ sending $[X]$ to $\sum (-1)^ i[H(X[i])]$. </p>
